fault"}], "shared_items": [{"id": "SI1", "text": "both conventions are documented and on file"}, {"id": "SI2", "text": "the four stages and the six-week date"}, {"id": "SI3", "text": "the fact that both cannot govern one stage"}], "available_options": [{"id": "AO1", "text": "written sign-off throughout"}, {"id": "AO2", "text": "in-meeting throughout"}, {"id": "AO3", "text": "alternating by stage"}, {"id": "AO4", "text": "a hybrid drafted for this deliverable only"}], "available_routes": [{"id": "AR1", "text": "this session"}], "agreement_contents": [{"id": "AC1", "text": "which convention governs which stage"}, {"id": "AC2", "text": "what the stage gate requires"}, {"id": "AC3", "text": "what is filed"}], "counterpart_role": "The two group representatives.", "counterpart_position": "Each holds a documented convention.", "difference_established": "Two documented conventions that cannot both govern a stage.", "authority_relation": "Peers; the program office records.", "recording_route": "The convention note on file.", "persistence_point": "The first stage gate.", "exchange_test_point": "B6", "list_note": "Not selectable in available_routes, because only the session itself completes and is evidenced inside the session; a route the participant can only state is an intention: a written convention note for the deliverable; to the program office.", "source_note": "Re-framed from the library scenario: The library scenario is built on a clash attributed to national or organizational culture. every cultural attribution is removed and none may be restored. No nationality, region, background or organization type appears anywhere in this source. What remains is two documented working conventions on one deliverable, each established as documented practice and neither attached to any group. A source that asks A mentor to observe conduct against A cultural expectation cannot produce A fair record.", "situation_class_label": "Two parties holding different positions on a decision bot